<font size="3"><b>RAIDING FOR DUMMIES</b></font><br/><br/><b>Getting to the raid:</b> Do your best to arrive at scheduled raids by the time they are scheduled to begin. Arriving late only serves to waste the time of your friends. If you do not know how to get to the raid destination, find out before the raid is called! Maps can be downloaded if needed or you can travel with people that know the way!<br/><br/><b>Chat:</b> Use /rsay for useful raid related information only. Limit your spam in group. Inessential chat, jokes and similar banter belong in the Halcyons chat channel. Always think before you speak, both about what you say and in which channel you say it!<br/><b><br/>AFK on raids: </b>It is wisest to avoid going AFK on raids for more than a few seconds! However, we know that sometimes life happens! When you go AFK make sure you put up the tag (/afk). Auto-follow (/follow) a group member who is likely to stay in the back lines (a caster). If you need to go AFK for more than two minutes, it is best to pass group leadership (if you have it) to someone else in group. Please dont burden and abuse your group by making a habit of ninja AFKing. Members who make a habit of doing so will be disciplined.<br/><br/><b>Group Leader Exp:</b> It is typically best etiquette to give group leadership to the person who has the largest number of useful GLExp points. A raid is NOT the place to work on leadership experience, so please be gracious when asked to submit group leadership to someone with more abilities to benefit your group. The most useful GLExp points on raids are: HoTT, HE, OE and ME.<br/><br/><b>Assist:</b> /assist off… ALWAYS. Know who the main assist is and always assist them! Pay close attention to &quot;Unmezzable&quot; messages from the enchanters and watch for &quot;Change target&quot; commands from the Raid Leader or Main Assist.<br/><br/><b>Arriving Late/Leaving Early: </b>Find out who the Raid leader is and let them know if you are arriving late or leaving early. Your presence may be vital to the raid strategy planned and foreknowledge of your absence or presence during the encounter is essential! Ask the raid leader how to get to the raid. Sometimes a CoH will be set up, sometimes it is easiest to die and have a rogue drag you.<br/><b><br/>Training the Raid:</b> Don't. <br/><br/><b>Push:</b> The &quot;Push&quot; is a raid occurence that we wish to avoid! Every time you hit a mob (melee especially, but spells too), it is pushed ever so slightly away from you! On a raid, when 10 people and pets are attacking a mob, it is easy to push the mob anywhere in the zone.<br/><br/>Pushing often wipes raids EASILY in one of three major ways.<br/><br/>1) Push a mob into adds, adds kill clerics, raid dies.<br/>2) Push a mob with nasty AE into casters (or position one so frontal AE's hit casters), casters die (or in some cases, are silenced) and raid wipes.<br/>3) Push a mob one step too far and MT is oor for CHeal.<br/><br/><b>Avoiding &quot;The Push&quot;</b><br/><br/>You cannot avoid pushing mobs unless you do not attack them. How can we avoid tragedies? Offset the push by moving!! If you notice a mob is being pushed terribly to the west, go to the west side of the mob and push it east! It is well worth losing those 5 seconds of you attacking in order to keep the mob in the position we like it! <br/><br/>As well, casters can contribute to positioning by facing the direction in which the mob needs to be pushed when nuking, in effect working with the pushback of nukes to help position the mob.<br/><br/><b>Buffs:</b> In a raid setting you will NOT have all the buffs you have in typical group settings.  Buffs will be done a few minutes after the rally call and before pulls begin.  For most of Halcyon's pre-Time raids, MGB'd level 65 spells are sufficient.<br/><br/>  What buffs should you expect?  <br/>  Symbol of Balikor<br/>  Aura of reverence<br/>  Steeloak<br/>  Clairvoyance<br/>  Speed of Salik<br/>  Focus of Woushi<br/>  Talisman of Fortitude<br/>  Brells Brawny Barrier<br/>  Spirit of the Predator<br/>  Spiritual Ascendance<br/><br/>**special case: Paladins and Conviction- find out which cleric will have conviction up and send tells to that cleric as you need it.**<br/><br/>What if you missed the buffs or are dispelled or are not rebuffed after a death?<br/><br/>Use /who commands to find out which buffers are in the zone (this is ONE reason why you are not /roleplay or /anon on a raid).  /tell one person from the class that casts your needed buff that you need that buff (do not use /rsay, /guild, /group or /halcyons for buff requests).<br/><br/>Can you always send tells for buffs?<br/><br/>NO!  Before the encounter is triggered or pulled, the raid leader will provide a short time for clerics to med and everyone to check their buffs.  At this time, please use the alt key to see how much time is left on your buffs.  If there is less than 5 minutes on a buff, send a /tell for a rebuff!  Once an event or a raid-target is incoming, DO NOT send any buff requests.  Tells during raid encounters are distracting to people who are concentrating on other things.<br/>
